<title>POLAND: Polish wheat prices down, rye/barley up last week.</title>
<headline>Polish wheat prices down, rye/barley up last week.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement that the average price of wheat fell while rye and barley prices rose at last week's grain auctions.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to Nov 2    previous week    yr/yr change</p>
<p>   Wheat	63.63 zl/q	 64.01 zl/q	  N/A</p>
<p>   Rye	  43.68 zl/q	 43.29 zl/q	  N/A</p>
<p>   Barley     54.00 zl/q	 53.68 zl/q	  N/A</p>
<p>zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>--Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
